From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 14:01:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ether: disable PMF so the WPA handshake can complete

WiFi associates and the WPA 4-way handshake never completes on 20.0:

    SupplicantStaNetworkHalAidlImpl:  RequirePmf: false
    wpa_supplicant: wlan0: WPA: Selected AP supports MFP: require MFP
    wpa_supplicant: wlan0: Authentication with <bssid> timed out.
    wpa_supplicant: wlan0: WPA: 4-Way Handshake failed - pre-shared key may be incorrect

The framework asks for RequirePmf=false, but the AOSP template sets a global pmf=1 (MFP optional) and
wpa_supplicant upgrades that to *required* whenever the AP advertises MFP capability. The
prima/qcacld driver on msm8992 does not handle PMF, so msg 3/4 never arrives and the handshake times
out. "pre-shared key may be incorrect" is wpa_supplicant's generic timeout message, not a key
mismatch -- it failed against a phone hotspot too.

19.1 ships the same pmf=1 template and works, because it used the HIDL supplicant HAL; 20.0 uses
AIDL, new in A13, where RequirePmf=false does not reach the network block as ieee80211w=0.

Cost: no WPA3-SAE, which requires PMF. This driver cannot do WPA3 anyway.
---
 wifi/wpa_supplicant_overlay.conf | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/wifi/wpa_supplicant_overlay.conf b/wifi/wpa_supplicant_overlay.conf
index d6ae451..902c6a1 100644
--- a/wifi/wpa_supplicant_overlay.conf
+++ b/wifi/wpa_supplicant_overlay.conf
@@ -4,3 +4,27 @@ tdls_external_control=1
 bss_max_count=512
 bss_no_flush_when_down=1
 driver_param=use_p2p_group_interface=1
+
+# Disable 802.11w / PMF (Protected Management Frames).
+#
+# WiFi associates but the WPA 4-way handshake never completes on 20.0:
+#
+#   SupplicantStaNetworkHalAidlImpl:  RequirePmf: false
+#   wpa_supplicant: wlan0: WPA: Selected AP supports MFP: require MFP
+#   wpa_supplicant: wlan0: Authentication with <bssid> timed out.
+#   wpa_supplicant: wlan0: WPA: 4-Way Handshake failed - pre-shared key may be incorrect
+#   wpa_supplicant: wlan0: State: 4WAY_HANDSHAKE -> DISCONNECTED
+#
+# The framework asks for RequirePmf=false, but the AOSP template sets a global
+# pmf=1 (MFP optional) and wpa_supplicant upgrades that to *required* whenever
+# the AP advertises MFP capability. The prima/qcacld driver on msm8992 does not
+# handle PMF, so msg 3/4 never arrives and the handshake times out. The
+# "pre-shared key may be incorrect" line is wpa_supplicant's generic timeout
+# message, not an actual key mismatch -- it failed against a phone hotspot too.
+#
+# 19.1 ships the same pmf=1 template and works, because it used the HIDL
+# supplicant HAL; 20.0 uses AIDL (new in A13), where RequirePmf=false does not
+# reach the network block as ieee80211w=0.
+#
+# Cost: no WPA3-SAE, which requires PMF. This driver cannot do WPA3 anyway.
+pmf=0
